D.tail_replace("All hosts: the native bootstrap scripts", "The pull request workflow `.github/workflows/build-system.yml` has two jobs", "The workflow `.github/workflows/build-system.yml` runs on every pull request, every push to `main` and by hand, with `contents: read` only, one concurrency group per pull request or ref (a newer push cancels a running pull request run) and every action pinned to a commit SHA. Its two jobs run on `ubuntu-latest` (X64), `macos-latest` (ARM64) and `windows-latest` (X64). `smoke` (60 minutes) enables long paths before the checkout on Windows, checks that `packageManager` and `engines.node` of `package.json` equal the workflow pins and that the runner architecture equals the architecture of the pinned Bun asset, installs Bun 1.4.2 with a verified SHA-256 (no installer script), and runs `bun repo --help`, `preflight` and `tools setup all`. The Bun store is restored into `.cache/b/d/m/bun-cache` only after `tools setup all` because the partition has to be attached first (key from `bun.lock`, `*/bun.lock` and `package.json`). After `dependencies sync --all` the job proves the cache of both tools on `@teaching/architecture-course:test`: `cache clear`, one run (the entries and bytes of `cache status` must grow), a second run (the entries must not grow, and the run must be recognised as a hit: for Nx the output says it read from the cache, for Bazel it shows `disk cache hit` or `remote cache hit`, or the first run spawned work, the second spawned none and the build completed). `products` (90 minutes, after `smoke`) restores the Bun store and the Bazel disk cache `.cache/b/p/m/bazel/actions` (key from `MODULE.bazel`, `.bazelversion`, `.bazelrc` and `bun.lock` plus the commit, the key prefix as fallback) and runs that target under `--tool=nx` and `--tool=bazel`. Caches are saved only by pushes to the default branch (the Bun store by `smoke`, the Bazel disk cache by `products`), so a pull request cannot evict them. It uses no `sudo` and no installer; `actionlint` 1.7.7 reports no finding on it and the pinned action SHAs and the Bun SHA-256 values matched upstream when they were written. The course release workflow `architecture-course.yml` is separate and manual. Not yet verified: the workflow has never run, so the Bazel hit rule (a calibrated reading of Bazel's console summary), the two cache restores into the owned partitions and the Windows and Linux legs are untested; and under the current adapter a Bazel second run is not expected to hit (see Bazel implementation, Source link and `.bazelignore`).", "en")

