# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cache partitions
D.insert_after("`.cache/b/c` is the plain control directory", [
"",
"**macOS volume silence.** macOS logs file system events of every mounted volume to `.fseventsd` and indexes it; on an image that only a build tool writes this fills the 63 MiB leases image and the small partitions. Each image therefore carries `.fseventsd/no_log` and `.metadata_never_index` (protocol constants in `🧰️framework/🔨️modules/🏃️process/📦️artifacts/🏗️native-build/💾️storage/🍎️image/🤫️silence/🧬️schema/🔣️.json`). A write after mount does not work: with `-owners on` macOS creates `.fseventsd` as `root:staff 0700` with an ACL, and a log keeps growing until the volume is detached and attached again. So the images are created from a seed folder (`hdiutil create -format UDRW -srcfolder <seed> -size … -nospotlight` yields the same fixed image as `-type UDIF`, with the markers user-owned from the start), and `applyNativeImageVolumeSilenceV1` runs on attach and again whenever an already mounted image is opened: it creates the directory and the markers if they are missing and prunes old logs (regular single-link files named by 16 hexadecimal digits, in batches of 64) once more than 8 files or 1 MiB remain. A root-owned or symlinked `.fseventsd` and non-regular markers are refused with a remedy. A silenced volume has no FSEvents service, so the publication witness treats it as a volume without a service domain (`observeNativeVolumeEventServiceV1` returns `null`). Capacity: APFS holds 40,960 bytes less than the image, and 200 MiB less when the image is larger than 2 GiB (measured on 15 images from 32 MiB to 4,095 MiB), so every partition exposes `usableBytes` and for partitions up to 256 MiB the logical limit must fit it; that is why `leases.maximumLogicalBytes` is 62,914,560 of 67,108,864. Observed on 2026-10-20: the live images were mounted before their markers existed and macOS keeps logging until each partition is detached and attached again; after the open-time repair `.fseventsd` of `d`, `l` and `g` held 3, 5 and 1 entries (the dependencies image had held about 200 logs before), and every partition has `.metadata_never_index`. Not yet verified: a freshly created seeded image through the whole `tools setup` path, and the seeded creation on another macOS version.",
], "en")

D.insert_after("7. **`dependencies sync` fails with `EPERM", [
"8. **`.fseventsd` of a partition grows to hundreds of 16-digit log files, or a small image reports ENOSPC**: the volume was mounted before it was silenced. Any command that opens the partition prunes the residue. To stop the logging at its source, detach and attach the partition when nothing runs (macOS: the commands of item 2, then `bun repo --help`); a root-owned `.fseventsd` is refused by design and has to be removed with `sudo` by hand.",
], "en")

